NC(1)                        User Commands

NAME
    nc - TCP and UDP client and server

SYNOPSIS
    nc [-u] HOST PORT
    nc [-u] -l PORT

DESCRIPTION
    Connects to HOST:PORT (or with -l accepts one connection on PORT) and
    relays standard input to the peer and the peer's data to standard
    output. End of input half-closes the TCP connection; the command ends
    when the peer closes. With -u datagrams are exchanged instead; a
    listening UDP server answers the first peer it hears from, and the
    command runs until interrupted. Ports are numeric. Connection and
    resolver failures are reported with their reason.

SEE ALSO
    http(1), ping(1), index(7)
